# LXDE session autostart
#
# Copied into each session home on first run. These entries are executed by
# lxsession in order. The two LXDE components below are mandatory - without
# them there is no panel and no desktop.
#
# The stock Debian file also starts xscreensaver, which is intentionally not
# installed here: an idle screensaver is a liability in a VNC session, and the
# logout menu's lock action (lxlock) covers manual locking.

@lxpanel --profile LXDE
@pcmanfm --desktop --profile LXDE

# Keep the desktop alive: if pcmanfm --desktop dies, the icons, the wallpaper
# and the desktop context menu disappear.
sh -c 'while true; do pgrep -f "pcmanfm --desktop" >/dev/null || pcmanfm --desktop --profile LXDE; sleep 5; done'
